  "source": "[\\(uniformly.continuous)::real.function:on{U}]\nRefines: f\nwhen: U \\:subset:/ \\reals..R\nspecifies: f is \\function:on{U}:to{\\reals..R}\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: eps is \\real\n  where: eps \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n  then:\n  . exists: delta is \\real\n    suchThat:\n    . delta \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n    . forAll: x, y is \\real\n      where:\n      . x \"in\" U\n      . y \"in\" U\n      . \\real.abs(x \\.real.-./ y) \\:real.less?:/ delta\n      then: \\real.abs(f(x) \\.real.-./ f(y)) \\:real.less?:/ eps\nDocumented:\n. adjective: \"uniformly continuous\"\n. description: \"A function is uniformly continuous if a single $\\delta$ works\n                across the entire domain.\"\nId: \"f69d925b-5ae6-4969-9d22-4d4eeea90a08\"",
